### LEAD 5: Staging directory server exposure

**Source hypothesis:** `ds-apip.test.threema.ch`, `apip.test.threema.ch` publicly reachable with identical API surface + CORS `*`. HSTS/Expect-CT on staging but not production. Confidence: 60–65.

| Q | Answer | Reasoning |
|---|--------|-----------|
| Q1 | **NO** | `scope.yml` lists `apip.threema.ch` (production). Staging `.test` variants are not listed. |
| Q2 | YES | Publicly reachable. |
| Q3 | LOW | Mirrors production data (identical pubkeys for `ECHOECHO`). No additional attack surface beyond production directory, which is by-design public. |
| Q4 | YES | Passive. |
| Q5 | NO | Not novel. |
| Q6 | **FAIL** | Out of scope. Also falls under info disclosure of public data (same as Lead 1). |
| Q7 | NO | Out of scope; mirrors production which is already invalid. |

**Verdict: INVALID** — Out of scope (staging not in `scope.yml`); mirrors production which is by-design public directory.

